WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.620
Public feuds, day drinking, and sexual assault:
With great fame comes great entitlement, and

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.780
some of Hollywood's finest are just downright
jerks.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.000
As Kendall Roy on HBO's "Succession," Jeremy
Strong stars in one of the biggest shows on television.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.590
But as his career has been on a massive upswing,
his reputation amongst his fellow actors has

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.940
taken a bit of a hit.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:26.019
Though he rejects the label himself, Strong
is frequently described as a method actor.

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:30.210
Phenomenal results can be achieved by remaining
in character in this fashion, but the tactics

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.950
of method actors often rub crew members and
castmates the wrong way.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.370
One notorious profile on Strong in "The New
Yorker" struck a particularly powerful blow

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.349
to his public reputation.

00:00:40.349 --> 00:00:45.180
The profile revealed that while shooting "Succession,"
he was prone to preparing rehearsed speeches

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.830
and trying to pass them off as improvisation,
as well as getting inebriated on set when

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.549
his character fell off the wagon.

00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:56.539
His castmates have described his method acting
approach as occasionally frustrating or intrusive,

00:00:56.539 --> 00:01:00.899
but none have been more vocally opposed to
his habits than Brian Cox, who plays Strong's

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:03.020
on-screen father Logan Roy.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:07.189
During an interview with "Town &amp; Country,"
Cox said that he thinks Strong is a fantastic

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:11.050
actor but that he finds his method acting
style to be annoying.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.549
"Succession" is far from the only production
where Strong's method acting has been an impediment

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:16.280
for others.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.600
On "The Trial of the Chicago 7," he frequently
ruined takes by pulling pranks while in character

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.040
as hippie Jerry Rubin.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.810
And for one scene, he requested to be blasted
with real tear gas, even though that would

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:32.070
have meant putting hundreds of extras and
crew members through the same physical torment.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.280
Gérard Depardieu is one of the most celebrated
actors in the history of French cinema.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.290
Having nearly 250 credits in his filmography
over the course of five decades, Depardieu

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.130
has played many iconic and acclaimed roles.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:48.590
With such superstardom inflating his ego,
he has been known to act as if the rules didn't

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.539
apply to him.

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:53.780
Depardieu committed petty crime in his youth,
and he's had plenty of brushes with the law

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.630
after becoming a star as well.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.290
"Did you steal?"

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.410
"Steal?

00:01:58.410 --> 00:01:59.490
Yes, of course."

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:03.960
His scandals ran the gamut from physical assault
and frequent fighting to white-collar crimes

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.609
connected to his numerous businesses to a
weird incident in which he urinated on a plane.

00:02:08.609 --> 00:02:11.780
"You were flying to Ireland—"
"Yes, I peed on the plane.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.560
Yes."

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.800
During the #MeToo movement, Depardieu was
accused of sexual assault by more than a dozen

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.790
women, most of whom were actors or crew members
who worked with him.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:27.540
As reported by the "Associated Press," 13
accusers came out against him while also suggesting

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.780
that his total number of victims was surely
much higher since he had a reputation for

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.300
frequently groping and fondling the extras
on his film shoots.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.390
Depardieu has often been hailed as one of
the greatest actors of his generation, but

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.599
incredible performances don't justify his
actions by any stretch of the imagination.

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:49.290
Tommy Lee Jones is a four-time Oscar nominee
and one-time winner for his role in 1994's

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.680
"The Fugitive."

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.970
He is known less for his range and more for
his reliability when it comes to playing rugged,

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.360
ornery characters.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.800
The dial can shift from violent and intense,
such as in films like "The Hunted," to comedically

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.739
slanted, as we see in "Men in Black."

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:06.640
Regardless, the same core archetype of a curmudgeon
is usually present.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.750
And as it turns out, this baseline character
type is close to home for Jones.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.080
In a 2006 edition of "Texas Monthly," the
actor was profiled in a piece titled "Tommy

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.970
Lee Jones is Not Acting," which posited that
he really is the rude and grumpy fellow that

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.849
he routinely plays on screen.

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:27.440
He is known to be incredibly impolite to the
press and the general public, and that behavior

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.060
extends to film sets.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.420
When Jim Carrey appeared on "Norm MacDonald
Live," he recounted his experiences working

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.930
with Jones on "Batman Forever."

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.690
"He said to me he couldn't sanction my buffoonery."

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:44.010
Tobey Maguire is best known for starring as
Spider-Man in the Sam Raimi trilogy, and he

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.549
recently reprised the role in "Spider-Man:
No Way Home."

00:03:46.549 --> 00:03:52.030
The heroic, morally upright side of the character
is allegedly not one shared by Maguire personally.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:56.140
For many years, the actor has had a reputation
for being hard to work with and extremely

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.790
troublesome behind the scenes.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:02.360
His rude, out-of-control behavior on sets
has drawn fire from his co-stars, and his

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.380
public outbursts captured by paparazzi have
hurt his image with the general public.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:11.090
Maguire is one of the only successful Hollywood
stars to be so incendiary in real life that

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:16.220
he became the villain of a woman's non-fiction
autobiography and its corresponding film adaptation.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:21.790
The 2017 film "Molly's Game" tells the true
story of Molly Bloom, who ran high-stakes

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.970
poker games for Hollywood celebrities.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.710
In the film, Michael Cera plays an antagonist
who goes by 'Player X.'

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.920
He makes it his mission to destroy Bloom's
reputation and livelihood while also being

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.710
as awful as possible to his fellow players
at every turn.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:39.389
Though the character's true identity remains
unnamed in the movie, Bloom names him outright

00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:42.130
as Tobey Maguire in her autobiography.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:46.400
Dustin Hoffman has given some of the best
and most influential performances of all time.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.600
His roles in films like "The Graduate" and
"Midnight Cowboy" were instrumental in ushering

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.130
in the New Hollywood movement, completely
changing the film industry of the late 1960s

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.280
and 1970s.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:00.530
One of his most acclaimed films was "Kramer
vs. Kramer," in which he plays a husband who

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.700
is left in charge of his young son when his
wife leaves him.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.120
Hoffman earned his first Oscar win for the
role, but his methods for achieving that performance

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.810
were questionable, to say the least.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:14.430
Hoffman was engaging in hardcore method acting
for the role and took it upon himself to force

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.900
what he considered to be a stronger performance
out of co-star Meryl Streep, who also won

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.580
her first Oscar for the film.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.289
While indulging in frequent improvisation,
Hoffman slapped Streep, smashed a real glass

00:05:25.289 --> 00:05:29.610
against a wall right beside her head without
warning, and made low-blow insults about her

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.840
recently-deceased boyfriend, actor John Cazale.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:33.680
"I'm leaving you."

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.180
"Honey, please.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.180
I can't hear."

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.490
Far worse than all of his nasty on-set behavior,
however, are the numerous sexual assault allegations

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:43.480
that have been made against Hoffman, as reported
in Forbes.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:47.699
His accusers came into contact with Hoffman
through film shoots and his theatrical performances

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:52.710
on Broadway, making working with him in any
capacity an unpleasant proposition.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:56.910
Jennifer Lopez has drawn acclaim for both
her music and her acting, as well as for having

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.370
led a successful career as a producer.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:04.100
Despite her legions of die-hard fans, Lopez's
reputation is far less sterling when it comes

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:07.740
to those who have to work with her, not just
enjoy her output from a distance.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:12.869
She has frequently been described as difficult
or outright impossible to work with professionally.

00:06:12.869 --> 00:06:17.880
Lopez has shown a tendency to lash out at
and insult other celebrities when giving interviews.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:22.849
One of the celebrities that Lopez was most
harsh towards was Cameron Diaz, in a now-infamous

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.190
interview with "Movieline."

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:28.139
When the two were cast alongside each other
in "What to Expect When You're Expecting,"

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:30.649
there was obviously a lot of animosity on
set.

00:06:30.649 --> 00:06:34.860
This was far from being an isolated incident,
as there are countless stories of her making

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:39.539
life harder for co-stars and crew members
and even members of the general public, such

00:06:39.539 --> 00:06:43.789
as a hotel maid who she reportedly had fired
for asking for an autograph.

00:06:43.789 --> 00:06:45.740
Lopez has since denied that claim.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.479
Lara Flynn Boyle's big breakout role was on
the one-of-a-kind television phenomenon "Twin Peaks."

00:06:50.479 --> 00:06:54.750
She played Donna Hayward, the best friend
of murder victim Laura Palmer.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:59.460
Boyle starred in both of the show's two seasons
before it was prematurely canceled by ABC.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.900
When the prequel movie, "Twin Peaks: Fire
Walk With Me," was released just one year

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:07.880
after the cancellation, Boyle was no longer
involved, although her character still was.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:12.340
The recasting of Donna Hayward with Moira
Kelly raised fan suspicions that behind-the-scenes

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:16.629
issues had led to Boyle's removal from "Twin
Peaks," especially considering the fact that

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:18.800
she was the only cast member replaced.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:23.090
When the 2017 revival of the series, "Twin
Peaks: The Return," finally came to fruition

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:27.580
many years later, Boyle publicly voiced her
desire to return to the series.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.970
Instead, creator David Lynch purposefully
excluded her, despite pretty much everyone

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:32.970
else returning.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:37.039
Her behind-the-scenes romances were considered
by some to be a hindrance to the series.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:41.430
According to an "AV Club" interview with Sherilyn
Fenn, she allegedly put a stop to the planned

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:45.480
romance between the Dale Cooper and Audrey
Horne characters because she was dating actor

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.390
Kyle MacLachlan in real life.

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:51.639
Boyle had a few other major roles outside
of "Twin Peaks," but as word spread of her

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:54.779
being difficult to work with, her good roles
dried up.

00:07:54.779 --> 00:07:59.590
These days, her acting gigs are few and far
apart, and frequently take the form of trashy

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:02.470
B-movies like "Hansel &amp; Gretel Get Baked."

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.699
Casey Affleck is the younger brother of fellow
actor Ben Affleck.

00:08:05.699 --> 00:08:09.610
The brothers have worked together many times
over the years, but Casey Affleck's career

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:12.169
took a bit longer to reach the heights of
his brother's.

00:08:12.169 --> 00:08:16.259
Still, many film critics considered him to
be the superior actor of the two, and the

00:08:16.259 --> 00:08:19.419
one who has consistently chosen more interesting
projects.

00:08:19.419 --> 00:08:23.750
His performances in movies like "The Assassination
of Jesse James by the Coward Robert Ford"

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:28.290
and "Manchester by the Sea" both drew widespread
acclaim, and the latter even earned him his

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.360
first Oscar win.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.360
"I'm sorry Lee.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.360
He passed away about an hour ago."

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:36.680
As reported by "The Daily Beast," Affleck
was accused of sexual harassment by multiple

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:41.200
women, including the cinematographer and a
producer of 2010's "I'm Still Here."

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.970
The accusations led to a pair of lawsuits
that Affleck settled out of court.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:49.480
On the same shoot, Affleck partially admitted
to creating an unsafe work environment and

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.950
that he was rarely sober throughout the production.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.460
According to "The Guardian," he encouraged
his cast and crew to party with him as part

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:57.790
of the mockumentary experience.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.370
Sean Penn is a five-time nominee and two-time
Oscar winner with many acclaimed performances

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:05.260
and even a few films as a director under his
belt.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:09.029
Over the years, he has developed something
of a negative reputation, a fact that Penn

00:09:09.029 --> 00:09:10.520
has knowingly embraced.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:14.730
In his Oscar acceptance speech for his performance
in 2008's "Milk," Penn said,

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.530
"I do know how hard I make it to appreciate
me."

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.970
Penn has also made it clear on other occasions
that he knows he can be difficult to work

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:24.360
with and even to simply interact with on a
personal level.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:28.370
He has been involved in many altercations
and blow-ups with the directors of his movies

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:32.420
and does not hesitate at all to voice his
opposition to their creative decisions.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.370
All of this is without even getting into his
tangled history of domestic abuse allegations

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.070
and violent altercations in the U.S. and abroad.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:44.070
And while some of them have been disputed
by all parties involved, the details remain murky.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:49.500
Morgan Freeman once held a reputation as a
kindhearted man, an upstanding member of society,

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.810
and a role model for all.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:55.829
Not many actors can claim to be typecast as
God and as the go-to default for narration

00:09:55.829 --> 00:09:58.550
with one of the most distinctive voices in
Hollywood.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:02.640
But after a long and storied career with a
gentle and beloved reputation, Freeman was

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.649
outed as a prolific predator.

00:10:04.649 --> 00:10:08.690
According to "CNN," the actor was accused
by at least eight women of sexual harassment

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.360
and groping on film sets.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:15.560
Though the news became public during the #MeToo
movement that began in 2017, his pattern of

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:19.770
inappropriate behavior was well-known by those
in the industry for years beforehand.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:24.810
A crew member on 2013's "Now You See Me" revealed
that the women on the shoot all knew to expect

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:28.430
unwelcome sexual remarks and touching whenever
he was on set.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.769
They even collectively decided to wear more
conservative clothing in the hopes of combatting

00:10:32.769 --> 00:10:33.970
his advances.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.810
Freeman is also known to make film shoots
trying ordeals for the directors he works

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:40.300
with, even in some of his most acclaimed roles.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:44.060
When shooting "The Shawshank Redemption,"
Freeman allegedly refused to do additional

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.570
takes or follow the script.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:49.570
He also forced the big final moments of the
film to be scrapped and changed because he

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:53.030
considered them, as he stated in an interview
with the "New York Daily News,"

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:56.919
"Sort of asinine, sort of cliched, sort of
unnecessary."

